<p>This week I created a custom build of the <a class="link-external" rel="external" href="https://github.com/be5invis/Iosevka">Iosevka</a> font. I’ve used <a class="link-external" rel="external" href="https://input.djr.com/">Input Mono</a> for a long time now, and was very happy with it. However, it was missing a few glyphs that I wanted to use. Moreover, I didn’t have a license for the Input font to use on e.g. my blog. Iosevka is <a class="link-external" rel="external" href="https://github.com/be5invis/Iosevka/blob/master/doc/custom-build.md">stupendously customizable</a>, so I thought I’d see if I could get something close to Input’s styles.</p>